# Drafted by Gemini (R17 rooms2b), edited.

~ l19_diagrams
Narrator: Parchment sheets cover the desk, inked with alchemical ratios and crossed out in neat, tireless revisions. The margin notes smell faintly of dried lavender and cold lake water.
* [Arcana DC 12] Study them -> l19_study_ok | l19_study_fail
* Leave the notes alone -> END

~ l19_study_ok
Narrator: The script yields its secret to {name}: the Lethic Serum is distilled from the White Worm's ichor, and here, tucked in the final margin, is the exact recipe for its antidote.
set mr_antidote_known
set mr_truth_clues += 1
if flag.mr_truth_clues >= 2 and (quest.all_is_well == find_the_cousin or quest.all_is_well == sign_in)
quest all_is_well the_truth
endif
quest the_lethic_antidote learned
-> END

~ l19_study_fail
Narrator: The cramped notations and shifting measurements blur together, keeping their quiet alchemy to themselves.
-> END

~ l19_shrine
Narrator: A quiet alcove holds a wedding portrait, a blood-stained knight's tabard bearing a rising sun, a faded love sonnet, a betrothal ring, a phial of Unrefined Ichor, and a porcelain mask worked with violet filigree.
* [if not flag.lethica_mementos_carried and not flag.godlee_mementos_destroyed] Take the mementos -> l19_take
* [if not flag.mr_ring_taken] Take the ring and mask -> l19_ring
* [if not flag.mr_phial_taken] Take the phial -> l19_phial
* Leave them -> END

~ l19_take
Narrator: You gather the portrait, the stained tabard, and the soft paper of the old sonnet, lifting years of private grief from the shelf.
give mr_memento_portrait
give mr_memento_tabard
give mr_memento_sonnet
set lethica_mementos_carried
set mr_has_memento
-> l19_shrine

~ l19_ring
Narrator: The silver band and the cold porcelain mask slip into your keeping, light as a held breath.
give ring_of_protection
give mask_of_lethica_nightborne
set mr_ring_taken
-> l19_shrine

~ l19_phial
Narrator: You lift the small glass phial; the pale, thick ichor inside shifts sluggishly against the stopper.
set mr_phial_taken
set unrefined_ichor += 1
-> l19_shrine

~ l20_unit
Narrator: Copper pipes and violet-glass conduits converge upon a hissing pressure cylinder beneath heavy iron levers. The whole room hums like a wasp trapped in a jar.
* [if not flag.mr_engineering_broken and not flag.mr_lockdown] Throw the lever OFF (Lockdown) -> l20_off
* [if flag.mr_lockdown] Throw the lever ON, ending Lockdown -> l20_on
* Smash the unit -> l20_smash
* Leave -> END

~ l20_off
Narrator: The iron lever clanks down, the violet glow drains from the glass tubes, and heavy locks thud shut along the corridors.
set mr_lockdown
-> END

~ l20_on
Narrator: The cylinder sighs as the conduits drink their fill again, and the low violet hum returns to the walls.
set mr_lockdown_over
set mr_lockdown = 0
-> END

~ l20_smash
Narrator: Glass shatters and the memory of years pours out as a gibbering mouther of violet ooze, babbling a thousand bad memories at once.
set mr_engineering_broken
combat mr_mouthers

~ l21_file
Narrator: A thick woven mat and empty wooden bowls sit upon the floor of this quiet den, while glass vials rest on a high shelf above.
* Take the stabilizer vials -> l21_vials
* [Perception DC 15] Look under the mat -> l21_file_ok | l21_file_miss
* Leave -> END

~ l21_vials
Narrator: You reach up to the high shelf and pocket the heavy glass vials of stabilizer.
give mr_stabilizer_stone
give mr_stabilizer_acid
give mr_stabilizer_stim
-> l21_file

~ l21_file_ok
Narrator: Beneath the woven rushes, {name} uncovers a leather folder charting Hugo's surgeries, his old curse, and how the treatments keep him dependent.
give mr_hugo_file
set mr_hugo_file_read
-> l21_file

~ l21_file_miss
Narrator: Nothing catches {name}'s eye beneath the coarse weave of the mat.
-> l21_file

~ l22_chamber
Narrator: A broad glass chamber fogged with warm breath holds a pacing, fleshy abomination, while shelves of pickled brains float in pale jars along the wall.
* Collect noetic extract from the jars -> l22_extract
* Open the chamber's door -> l22_release
* Leave -> END

~ l22_extract
Narrator: You draw off the cold, pearlescent fluid from the specimen jars before stoppering them tight.
if not flag.mr_extract_taken
set mr_extract_taken
set noetic_extract += 4
endif
-> l22_chamber

~ l22_release
Narrator: The heavy latch gives way with a wet hiss, and the hungry thing inside lunges into the room.
set mr_otyugh_freed
combat mr_otyugh
